#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133390 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"}] :question/id #uuid "bb2795c3-6359-50d8-9531-1e9dfae7a2ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-10994" :question/problem "Find $5\\det(A)-\\det(B)$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & \\sqrt{13} & 4 \\\\ 4 & 11 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 9 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & \\sqrt{13} & 4 \\\\ 4 & 11 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 9 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n- Since $B$ is a diagonal matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal:\n$\\det(B) = 3 \\cdot (-4) \\cdot (-2) = 24$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5\\det(A)-\\det(B) = 5 \\cdot 0 - 24 = -24\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133391 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/id #uuid "dc780837-b763-5ba9-981a-2373afcb524a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10995" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0$?\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has proportional rows:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$\nAs a result, $\\mid A \\mid = 0$.\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, so\n$\\mid B \\mid = (-1) \\cdot 4 \\cdot (-3) = 12 \\neq 0$.\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero row:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nAs a result, $\\mid C \\mid = 0$.\n\nTherefore, only $\\mid A \\mid$ and $\\mid C \\mid$ are equal to $0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133392 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/id #uuid "33ca37e5-c598-52a2-861f-2d5bfa6fd571" :question/math-academy-id "e-10996" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $\\mid A|=0$.\n\n1. $A$ has a zero column\n2. $A$ has proportional rows\n3. $A$ has identical columns" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n- $A$ has proportional rows:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9217d280-f50a-53b0-bfc2-c0c7677a7699" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132351} {:answer/id #uuid "af4d8744-717f-5b80-8929-7c16169609f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132352} {:answer/id #uuid "e464b671-4764-5aea-be6a-a4532655d864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132353} {:answer/id #uuid "ef869476-3fb8-579b-b83e-4b14f4f5a083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132354} {:answer/id 